#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/coast.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.coast.coast:134
msgid ""
"Draw shorelines. Specify the pen attributes for shorelines [Default pen is "
"``\"0.25p,black,solid\"``]. Shorelines have four levels; by default, the "
"same pen is used for all levels. To specify the shoreline level, use the "
"format *level*\\ /*pen*. Pass a sequence of *level*\\ /*pen* strings to draw "
"different shoreline levels with different pens. When specific level pens are "
"set, those not listed will not be drawn [Default draws all levels]. "
"``shorelines=True`` draws all levels with the default pen.  Choose from the "
"following shoreline levels:  - ``1``: Coastline - ``2``: Lakeshore - ``3``: "
"Island-in-lake shore - ``4``: Lake-in-island-in-lake shore  Example usage:  "
"- ``shorelines=True``: Draw all shoreline levels with default pen. - "
"``shorelines=\"0.5p,blue\"``: Draw all shoreline levels with a 0.5-point "
"blue   pen. - ``shorelines=\"1/0.5p,black\"``: Draw only coastlines with a "
"0.5-point black   pen. - ``shorelines=[\"1/0.8p,black\", \"2/0.4p,blue\"]``: "
"Draw coastlines with a   0.8-point black pen and lakeshores with a 0.4-point "
"blue pen."
msgstr ""

